{
  "raw": {
    "https://clarke.applicantpool.com/jobs/1334276": {
      "title": "Analytical Chemistry Adjunct",
      "description": "Analytical Chemistry Adjunct. Clarke University. Clarke University is seeking applications for an adjunct faculty position to teach Analytical Chemistry and lab (6 contact hours/week) for upper-level science students beginning January 2027 . This course is offered by the chemistry program and serves as a required course for the chemistry major. The position requires a master's degree or a doctorate in chemistry or a related science area. Candidates who are ABD will be considered. The preferred delivery of the course is in-person on the Clarke University campus in Dubuque, IA, but applications for instructors who can teach hybrid or online will also be considered. To apply, please upload the following documents online at http://clarke.applicantpool.com : letter of interest, curriculum vitae, unofficial transcripts from the highest graduate degree earned, and the contact information for three (3) people to serve as a reference. Confidential reference letters may be emailed to HRLetters@clarke.edu . Review of applications will begin immediately. Clarke University is committed to fostering a welcoming campus community that celebrates each person's unique contributions and promotes an inclusive learning environment. Accordingly, Clarke University does not discriminate against any employee or applicant for employment because of race, color, religion, sex (including pregnancy, gender identity, and sexual orientation), national origin, age, disability, or genetic information."
    },
    "https://clarke.applicantpool.com/jobs/1311953": {
      "title": "Business Adjunct Faculty",
      "description": "Business Adjunct Faculty. Clarke University. Clarke University is seeking applications for adjunct faculty to teach Principles of Management, Business Leadership and Communications, and Principles of Marketing, beginning in August 2026 . The position requires a master's or doctoral degree in Business or a related area. If hired, the instructor will be expected to teach face-to-face on the Clarke University campus in Dubuque, IA, with the option to offer a portion of the class(es) virtually. To apply, please upload the following documents online at http://clarke.applicantpool.com : letter of interest, curriculum vitae, statement of teaching philosophy, unofficial transcripts from the highest degree earned, and the contact information for three (3) people to serve as a reference. In addition, confidential reference letters may be emailed to HRLetters@clarke.edu . Review of applications will begin immediately. Clarke University is committed to fostering a welcoming campus community that celebrates each person's unique contributions and promotes an inclusive learning environment. Accordingly, Clarke University does not discriminate against any employee or applicant for employment because of race, color, religion, sex (including pregnancy, gender identity, and sexual orientation), national origin, age, disability, or genetic information."
    },
    "https://clarke.applicantpool.com/jobs/1322083": {
      "title": "Clinical Education Affiliates Coordinator",
      "description": "Clinical Education Affiliates Coordinator. Clarke University. At Clarke University, we look for individuals who lead from the heart and embrace our values of education, charity, justice, and freedom. By creating a community focused on care, we empower everyone at Clarke to do and be their best. We offer meaningful work, a safe and friendly work environment, and an outstanding benefits package. If you're looking for a place you can make a positive impact, we hope you'll consider Clarke! The University is currently seeking a qualified individual to assume the role of Clinical Education Affiliates Coordinator in the Physical Therapy Department . This is a 12-month full time position with approximately 40 hours per week. The Clinical Education Affiliates Coordinator is responsible for supporting the Director of Clinical Education (DCE), the Assistant DCE, Chair, and as needed, faculty within the Physical Therapy Department. Essential responsibilities include, but are not limited to: Maintain clinical education databases using Microsoft Access- including data entry, queries, and merging. Answer general questions related to clinical education sites from students, faculty, and clinical instructors. Assist in the planning and hosting of local and regional workshops for clinical instructors. Maintain student health records in compliance with HIPAA and FERPA in addition to monitoring site specific student health requirements and background checks. Assist PT Department Chair and ACCE with accreditation and program review process (tracking materials, formatting and editing final reports, etc.), correspondence, project work, and data collection and analysis. Provide administrative support to ACCE and Assistant ACCE for all activities related to clinical education such as correspondence, filing, managing contracts, arranging site visits, and management of clinical site information forms. Communicate with ACCE, Assistant ACCE, clinical education sites, and students. Maintain accurate and confidential information in an organized and accessible manner. Qualifications A High School diploma or GED is required, along with 1-3 years of general office experience. Preference given to individuals with a bachelor's degree and/or experience with databases- Microsoft Access in particular. The successful candidate must have demonstrated experience with MS Office products (Access, Word, Excel, PowerPoint) and excellent verbal and written communication skills. The ability to interact with a variety of departments, students, faculty and staff, and external clinical sites in a positive manner is critical. The candidate must have strong organizational skills with a desire to work independently. To apply for this position, please upload a cover letter and resume online at http://clarke.applicantpool.com/jobs . Resume review will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. Clarke University is committed to fostering a welcoming campus community that celebrates each person's unique contributions and promotes an inclusive learning environment. Accordingly, Clarke University does not discriminate against any employee or applicant for employment because of race, color, religion, sex (including pregnancy, gender identity, and sexual orientation), national origin, age, disability, or genetic information."
    },
    "https://clarke.applicantpool.com/jobs/1128524": {
      "title": "Custodian",
      "description": "Custodian. Clarke University. At Clarke University, we look for individuals who lead from the heart and embrace our values of education, charity, justice, and freedom. By creating a community focused on care, we empower everyone at Clarke to do and be their best. We offer meaningful work, a safe and friendly work environment, and an outstanding benefits package including tuition remission, paid holidays vacation and sick time, and extensive professional development opportunities. So, if you're looking for a place you can make a positive impact, we hope you'll consider our One Clarke, One Community. Clarke University is currently seeking a qualified individual to assume the role of Custodian. This is a full-time, first shift position. As a member of the Facilities Management team, this position will perform general housekeeping tasks in various campus buildings. Primary responsibilities include cleaning, scrubbing, mopping, sweeping, sanitizing, polishing and refilling consumable items. Qualifications include a high school diploma or GED equivalent with at least one year of custodial or related work experience. Candidate must be comfortable using cleaning supplies and other general maintenance tools (Ex. Ladders) and be comfortable with a moderate level of physical activity. The ability to work as an individual as well as within a team environment is required. Must be willing to successfully complete certification program. To apply, p lease upload your cover letter and resume online at http://clarke.applicantpool.com/jobs . Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Clarke University is committed to fostering a welcoming campus community that celebrates the unique contributions of each person and promotes an inclusive learning environment. Clarke University does not discriminate against any employee or any applicant for employment because of race, color, religion, sex (including pregnancy, gender identity, and sexual orientation), national origin, age, disability or genetic information."
    },
    "https://clarke.applicantpool.com/jobs/1317186": {
      "title": "General Maintenance",
      "description": "General Maintenance. Clarke University. At Clarke University, we look for individuals who lead from the heart and embrace our values of education, charity, justice, and freedom. By creating a community focused on care, we empower everyone at Clarke to do and be their best. We offer meaningful work, a safe and friendly work environment, and an outstanding benefits package. So, if you are looking for a place where you can make a positive impact, we hope you will consider Clarke. The university is currently seeking a qualified individual to join our facilities team in the role of General Maintenance. Primary responsibilities include, but are not limited to: Delivers packages, packaged goods, furniture, etc...to various locations. Performs general maintenance, including but not restricted to: Changing light bulbs/ballast Replacing ceiling tile Making minor plumbing repairs Replacing, repairing, and assisting in the installation of carpet, floor tile, and vinyl sheet goods. Assembling and maintaining furniture, equipment, and fixtures both indoors and outdoors Installing and/or replacing useable goods dispensers Minor repairs to windows including screens, locks, and glass. Assist in setting and breaking special events Carries on call pager in rotation with other maintenance personnel Cleans snow from assigned areas Grounds work as directed by manager Painting duties as directed by manager Qualifications include: The successful candidate must have: High school diploma and/or GED, and four years general maintenance experience in an institutional/industrial setting. To apply for this position, please upload a cover letter and resume online at http://clarke.applicantpool.com/jobs . Start date is negotiable. Clarke University is committed to fostering a welcoming campus community that celebrates the unique contributions of each person and promotes an inclusive learning environment. Clarke University does not discriminate against any employee or any applicant for employment because of race, color, religion, sex (including pregnancy, gender identity, and sexual orientation), national origin, age, disability or genetic information."
    },
    "https://clarke.applicantpool.com/jobs/1338468": {
      "title": "Graduate Assistant- Men's Soccer",
      "description": "Graduate Assistant- Men's Soccer. Clarke University. Clarke University invites applications for the graduate assistant coaching position in the men's soccer program to begin in January 2027. Responsibilities include assisting with the operation and management of the men's soccer program in accordance with university and NAIA philosophies. A bachelor's degree is required, and applicants must be admitted into a graduate degree program. To apply, upload a current resume and letter of interest at http://clarke.applicantpool.com . Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled."
    },
    "https://clarke.applicantpool.com/jobs/1334270": {
      "title": "Organic Chemistry Adjunct",
      "description": "Organic Chemistry Adjunct. Clarke University. Clarke University is seeking applications for an adjunct faculty position to teach Organic Chemistry II with lab (7 contact hours/week) for upper-level science students beginning January 2027 . Organic Chemistry II and lab are the second half of the two-semester sequence. These courses are offered by the chemistry program and serve as a required course for the biology and chemistry majors. The position requires a master's degree or a doctorate in chemistry or a related science area. Candidates who are ABD will be considered. The preferred delivery of the course is in-person on the Clarke University campus in Dubuque, IA, but applications for instructors who can teach hybrid or online will also be considered. To apply, please upload the following documents online at http://clarke.applicantpool.com : letter of interest, curriculum vitae, unofficial transcripts from the highest graduate degree earned, and the contact information for three (3) people to serve as a reference. Confidential reference letters may be emailed to HRLetters@clarke.edu . Review of applications will begin immediately. Clarke University is committed to fostering a welcoming campus community that celebrates each person's unique contributions and promotes an inclusive learning environment. Accordingly, Clarke University does not discriminate against any employee or applicant for employment because of race, color, religion, sex (including pregnancy, gender identity, and sexual orientation), national origin, age, disability, or genetic information."
    },
    "https://clarke.applicantpool.com/jobs/105202": {
      "title": "Security Officer- Part Time",
      "description": "Security Officer- Part Time. Clarke University. At Clarke University, everything we do is focused on making an impact on students so they can positively impact the world. For students, it means a place where more than facts are studied it means new ways of thinking are explored. For faculty and staff, it means more than just coming to work every day it means truly collaborating across the university to put student success first. It also means living and working in a thriving city named one of the \"most livable\" small cities in the country and one of \"Best Green Places\" in the country. The university is currently seeking qualified individuals to serve as part time Security Officers on the Campus Safety and Security team. These positions will work approximately 20 hours per week with variable shifts that will mostly be nights and weekends. Duties to include: following established rounds, monitoring security radio, enforcing parking regulations, opening and closing buildings and monitoring their mechanical operations, assisting police and fire depts. with any on campus incidents, writing security reports, and responding to service/emergency calls as needed. Occasional general light maintenance (changing light bulbs, changing smoke detector batteries, shoveling snow, etc.) will also be required. Hours will vary, but will primarily be nights and weekends . Position requires extensive walking in and outdoors in all weather conditions. Requirements: H.S. diploma, knowledge of procedures involved in building and grounds security work, valid drivers license, and strong customer service/communication skills. Direct experience in security and CPR, AED, first aid, or first responder certification preferred. (A criminal history background check will be completed prior to hire). To apply, please complete our online application at http://clarke.applicantpool.com/jobs . Please upload a current resume directly to this site along with contact information for three references."
    },
    "https://clarke.applicantpool.com/jobs/1340649": {
      "title": "Content and Web Strategist",
      "description": "Content and Web Strategist. Clarke University. At Clarke University, we look for individuals who lead from the heart and embrace our values of education, charity, justice, and freedom. By creating a community focused on care, we empower everyone at Clarke to do and be their best. We offer meaningful work, a safe and friendly work environment, and an outstanding benefits package. If you're looking for a place you can make a positive impact, we hope you'll consider Clarke! The university is currently seeking a qualified individual to assume the role of Content and Web Strategist. Under the direction of the Director of Marketing and Communication, this position plays a key role in developing compelling institutional content and managing the University's public-facing website. The successful candidate will be an exceptional writer and storyteller with strong digital communication skills, an eye for detail, and a passion for collaborating with campus partners to showcase the people, programs, and experiences that make Clarke distinctive. Primary Responsibilities Content Development and Storytelling: Develop, write, and edit engaging content for the University's website, publications, newsletters, marketing materials, and other communication channels. Identify and share compelling stories highlighting students, faculty, alumni, academic programs, and institutional achievements. Website Management: Oversee the University's public-facing website, ensuring content is accurate, accessible, engaging, and current. Collaborate with campus partners to maintain and improve website organization, navigation, usability, and overall effectiveness. Digital Content Optimization: Apply search engine optimization (SEO), digital accessibility, and website analytics best practices to strengthen the University's online visibility and improve audience engagement. Institutional Publications and Communications: Write and edit content for Clarke Magazine, recruitment materials, advancement communications, press releases, feature stories, and other institutional publications and announcements. Editorial Planning and Integrated Marketing: Develop and coordinate editorial calendars, content strategies, and messaging that support enrollment, fundraising, alumni engagement, and other University priorities. Collaborate with marketing colleagues to adapt content across print, digital, social media, and multimedia platforms. Campus Collaboration and Project Coordination: Partner with faculty, staff, and University leadership to identify communication opportunities, maintain consistent institutional messaging, and coordinate projects from concept through completion. Required Qualifications Excellent writing, editing, proofreading, and storytelling skills, with the ability to create engaging content for diverse audiences. Experience working with website content management systems and digital publishing tools. Strong organizational, project management, and interpersonal skills, with exceptional attention to detail and the ability to manage competing priorities, collaborate effectively across departments, and produce high-quality communications. Bachelor's degree in communication, journalism, English, marketing, public relations, or a related field. Preferred Qualifications Experience in higher education, nonprofit organizations, or other mission-driven environments. Experience developing editorial strategies, managing content calendars, and producing institutional publications or marketing communications. Knowledge of SEO, website analytics, digital accessibility, and website usability best practices. Familiarity with AP style, emerging digital communication trends, and AI-generated search technologies. To apply for this position, please upload a resume online at http://clarke.applicantpool.com . Resume review will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. Clarke University is committed to fostering a welcoming campus community that celebrates each person's unique contributions and promotes an inclusive learning environment. Accordingly, Clarke University does not discriminate against any employee or applicant for employment because of race, color, religion, sex (including pregnancy, gender identity, and sexual orientation), national origin, age, disability, or genetic information."
    },
    "https://clarke.applicantpool.com/jobs/1340648": {
      "title": "Director of Alumni Engagement and Annual Giving",
      "description": "Director of Alumni Engagement and Annual Giving. Clarke University. At Clarke University, we look for individuals who lead from the heart and embrace our values of education, charity, justice, and freedom. By creating a community focused on care, we empower everyone at Clarke to do and be their best. We offer meaningful work, a safe and friendly work environment, and an outstanding benefits package. If you're looking for a place you can make a positive impact, we hope you'll consider Clarke! The university is currently seeking a strategic, collaborative, and relationship-oriented professional to serve as its Director of Alumni Engagement and Annual Giving. Reporting to the Vice President for Institutional Advancement, this position provides leadership for the university's alumni engagement and annual fundraising programs, strengthening relationships with alumni, donors, and other constituents while advancing institutional philanthropic priorities. The Director develops and implements comprehensive engagement and fundraising strategies, leads major annual giving initiatives, and oversees alumni programs that foster lifelong connections with Clarke. The successful candidate will be an effective leader, skilled fundraiser, and enthusiastic relationship builder who values collaboration, creativity, and the opportunity to strengthen a culture of philanthropy within the University community. Key Responsibilities Strategic Leadership and Program Management: Develop and implement comprehensive alumni engagement and annual giving strategies, establish measurable goals, manage program budgets, and supervise the Assistant Director of Alumni Engagement and Annual Giving. Annual Giving and Fundraising Leadership: Lead annual fundraising campaigns, including Clarke Day, Giving Tuesday, and other institutional appeals. Develop targeted solicitation, donor acquisition, retention, and leadership giving strategies that strengthen philanthropic participation and revenue. Donor Cultivation and Relationship Development: Manage a portfolio of annual giving prospects, cultivating, soliciting, and stewarding donors through personalized outreach. Develop strategies to strengthen relationships with alumni, parents, employees, businesses, and other University constituents. Alumni Engagement and Volunteer Leadership: Direct alumni engagement programs, including Homecoming, reunions, regional gatherings, recognition programs, and volunteer initiatives. Serve as the primary liaison to the Alumni Association Board of Directors, supporting board leadership, engagement, and philanthropic priorities. Fundraising Events and Institutional Collaboration: Provide strategic leadership for the Clarke University Golf Classic and other major fundraising events. Collaborate with University leadership, Institutional Advancement colleagues, and campus partners to coordinate engagement, fundraising, and communication initiatives. Engagement and Fundraising Performance: Evaluate alumni engagement, donor participation, fundraising performance, and constituent feedback to strengthen strategies, improve program effectiveness, and maximize available resources. Required Qualifications Bachelor's degree in nonprofit management, marketing, communication, business, or a related field. Five or more years of progressively responsible professional experience in fundraising, alumni relations, nonprofit development, marketing, or a related field. Excellent communication, interpersonal, and relationship-building skills, with the ability to engage diverse constituents, collaborate with university leadership, and build effective partnerships. Strong leadership, organizational, and project management skills, with the ability to establish priorities, coordinate complex initiatives, manage competing responsibilities, and achieve measurable results. Proficiency with Microsoft Office applications and the ability to effectively manage constituent information, communications, and program activities. Preferred Qualifications Experience developing, managing, and evaluating fundraising campaigns, annual giving programs, or alumni engagement initiatives. Demonstrated experience cultivating, soliciting, and stewarding donors to strengthen philanthropic support and constituent relationships. Experience supervising professional staff, engaging volunteers, or working with nonprofit or alumni association boards. Familiarity with constituent relationship management (CRM) systems and fundraising platforms, such as Virtuous or GiveCampus, and using data to inform engagement and fundraising strategies. To apply for this position, please upload a resume online at http://clarke.applicantpool.com . Resume review will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. Clarke University is committed to fostering a welcoming campus community that celebrates each person's unique contributions and promotes an inclusive learning environment. Accordingly, Clarke University does not discriminate against any employee or applicant for employment because of race, color, religion, sex (including pregnancy, gender identity, and sexual orientation), national origin, age, disability, or genetic information."
    },
    "https://clarke.applicantpool.com/jobs/1340650": {
      "title": "Director of Marketing and Communication",
      "description": "Director of Marketing and Communication. Clarke University. At Clarke University, we look for individuals who lead from the heart and embrace our values of education, charity, justice, and freedom. By creating a community focused on care, we empower everyone at Clarke to do and be their best. We offer meaningful work, a safe and friendly work environment, and an outstanding benefits package. If you're looking for a place you can make a positive impact, we hope you'll consider Clarke! The university is currently seeking a collaborative and strategic leader to assume the role of Director of Marketing and Communication. Reporting to the Vice President for Institutional Advancement, this position provides leadership and strategic direction for the university's marketing, branding, and communication efforts. The Director will lead a team of marketing and communication professionals, establish departmental priorities, and develop integrated strategies that strengthen Clarke's reputation, support enrollment and fundraising, and advance institutional engagement. The successful candidate will be an effective people leader, strategic thinker, and skilled communicator who values collaboration, creativity, and the opportunity to advance the mission of a student-centered university. Primary Responsibilities Strategic Marketing and Communication Leadership: Develop and implement comprehensive marketing and communication strategies that advance institutional priorities, strengthen brand awareness, and support enrollment, fundraising, alumni engagement, and community relations. Department Leadership and Operations: Lead, mentor, and support Marketing and Communication staff while establishing clear priorities, effective workflows, and a collaborative, accountable team environment. Oversee departmental budgets, resource allocation, project management, and external vendor relationships. Brand Management and Institutional Communications: Provide strategic oversight of the University's brand identity, messaging, publications, media relations, and institutional communications, ensuring consistency and quality across communication channels. Partner with University leadership on major announcements, emerging issues, and crisis communications. Marketing Campaigns and Digital Strategy: Direct integrated marketing campaigns, advertising strategies, and digital communication initiatives. Provide strategic oversight of the university's website, social media presence, and digital marketing efforts, using performance data and emerging trends to inform decisions. Campus Collaboration and Strategic Partnerships: Serve as a strategic partner to university leadership and campus departments, identifying marketing and communication needs, coordinating institutional initiatives, and establishing collaborative planning processes. Marketing Effectiveness and Operational Excellence: Evaluate marketing effectiveness, departmental operations, and audience engagement through performance metrics and industry best practices, identifying opportunities to strengthen results, improve efficiency, and maximize available resources. Required Qualifications Demonstrated professional experience in marketing, communication, public relations, or a related field, including leadership of teams, projects, or organizational initiatives. Strong leadership, management, and organizational skills, with the ability to establish priorities, develop staff, manage resources, and navigate competing demands. Demonstrated ability to develop and implement strategic marketing and communication plans, including branding, digital marketing, and integrated campaigns. Excellent communication, interpersonal, and collaboration skills, with sound judgment and adaptability in working with university leadership, diverse stakeholders, and sensitive institutional matters. Bachelor's degree in marketing, communication, public relations, business, or a related field. Preferred Qualifications Experience supervising and developing professional staff, managing departmental budgets, coordinating external vendors, and overseeing integrated marketing initiatives. Experience in higher education, nonprofit organizations, or other mission-driven environments. Familiarity with marketing analytics, performance evaluation, and data-informed decision-making. To apply for this position, please upload a resume online at http://clarke.applicantpool.com . Resume review will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. Clarke University is committed to fostering a welcoming campus community that celebrates each person's unique contributions and promotes an inclusive learning environment. Accordingly, Clarke University does not discriminate against any employee or applicant for employment because of race, color, religion, sex (including pregnancy, gender identity, and sexual orientation), national origin, age, disability, or genetic information."
    }
